==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|spruce}} + {{term|up}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|spruces up|sprucing up|spruced up|}}

# {{idiom}} To dress or arrange [[smartly]], [[elegantly]], and [[neatly]]
# {{idiom}} To [[refresh]], [[revamp]]; to [[freshen]] or [[improve]] something, especially its [[appearance]]
#:''Fresh paint and some new curtains would do a lot to '''spruce up''' this dark room.

====Synonyms====
*[[spiff up]]